; FARO - Leo (player, the keeper's grandson) field sprites, 8x16 mode. Each 16x16 frame = 4 tiles: left pair (top, bottom),
; then right pair: frame base F -> OAM tiles F (left) and F+2 (right).
; Right-facing side frames only: flip X (S_FLIPX, and swap left/right pairs) for left.
; Walk: DOWN_A (stand) / DOWN_B (step); the other step = DOWN_B flipped X. Same for UP. SIDE_A/SIDE_B alternate.
; THROW = sling shot (side), FISH = rod cast (side, M2). 32 tiles = GDD budget (walk 24 + actions 8).
; Bike frames (M3) not drawn yet: they replace the 24 walk tiles through the tile queue.
; 32 tiles. Generated from a script, then this file is the source of truth.

